WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.610
- [Narrator] Seeking Secrets
is a social experiment

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.750
where strangers share
honest and complex truths.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.620
We ask that you treat the
participants with respect.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.670
Thank you for listening to their stories.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:21.160
- [Woman] My grandpa died
two years ago and I laughed

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.263
because he abused me when I was a child.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:32.516
- Um.
(intense music)

00:00:32.516 --> 00:00:34.860
(phone ringing)

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.663
- [Woman] You died, later.

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:39.659
She died.
- I hope one day

00:00:39.659 --> 00:00:41.326
I can see him again.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.690
- [Woman] When it comes
to death, for me at least,

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:54.650
I've always been very fearful
of it ever since I was younger

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:57.400
and not so much of
death, but the afterlife

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.110
because there's so many
different religions and beliefs,

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:05.830
and it was very scary to me to
not know which was for sure.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:08.240
When I was 16, my dad was murdered

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.330
and I just didn't feel, and to this day,

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:16.330
I hardly feel a spiritual
connection to him after he passed.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.650
So that kinda freaks me out too

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:20.910
because maybe there is reincarnation

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:24.070
and that's why I don't feel
their spirit or their presence.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:28.463
I don't feel that much pain
after a week of losing someone.

00:01:30.658 --> 00:01:32.470
- Well, she talked about
kind of losing her dad,

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.430
which really I guess,
struck a chord with me

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:36.050
just because I lost my dad.

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:39.100
She said at 16 and I lost my dad at 15.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:44.100
When she said that she
didn't feel a lot afterwards.

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:48.130
Typically when I think of
someone losing somebody,

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:52.290
I think of somebody going
through all the emotions.

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:53.860
- [Woman] When did you let yourself

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:56.883
start feeling those feelings of loss?

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:00.613
- Honestly? (laughs)

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:03.060
Sometimes I'm stuck at denial,

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.670
but it's only because I haven't
let myself think about it.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:06.740
When my grandma passed, it was like,

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:08.890
okay, you have to focus
on getting into college.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:11.110
Grandpa passed, it was still
like, okay, you're in college,

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:13.720
you have to keep going,
you can't fall behind.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:15.270
And then with my mom the same thing.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:18.900
And if I take that moment
to sit and really think

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:19.800
and let my emotions come out,

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:22.203
I'm scared that I'll be stuck there.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:26.570
- [Woman] Hi, I just
wanted to talk really quick

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:28.180
about my grandma.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:33.180
She just passed away and
it is a tremendous loss.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:36.760
When all of us were
going through her items

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:39.190
and deciding who would get what,

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:43.150
and seeing family members
fight over different things.

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:47.460
It just felt really,
really gross and icky.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:50.743
And we just felt like vultures, almost.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:57.280
- That one actually hit really
close to home right now.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.640
My grandmother's still alive.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:01.190
She's at that age where
she's really old already.

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:02.320
We're actually thinking about

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.730
what would happen to her things.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:04.980
And it sucks that a lot of it's

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.500
probably gonna get thrown away.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:09.300
My grandfather passed
away pretty suddenly,

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.150
and him and I were like best friends.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:14.720
When he passed away, my
grandma got rid of everything.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:16.220
I couldn't get anything from him.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:18.847
I have one article of clothing of his

00:03:18.847 --> 00:03:23.270
and a little oxygen tool that
he used for his oxygen mask.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.580
Like I have that, but that's, that's it.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:29.960
Seeing family and friends
fight over material things

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:33.780
when someone had just passed
away, that shouldn't matter.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.550
I wouldn't wanna give away her things.

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:38.443
'Cause I think about it too,
'cause she has so much stuff.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:42.583
And I'm actually really
not ready to lose her.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:46.853
I'm sorry, I love my grandma.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:55.180
- [Woman] When I was 19,
my mom was a heavy drinker.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:56.780
Ended up taking a lot of pills

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:59.150
that were legal, that were given to her

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:02.110
for her back pain and various reasons.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:06.440
The sad part is she was a
functioning mom, and alcoholic,

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:09.700
and you know, drug addict.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:13.560
Then one day she just
spiraled and moved out.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:17.590
I was so mad at her that
I wanted her to die.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:22.072
And I figured if she was
gone, life would be easier

00:04:22.072 --> 00:04:23.910
and there would be less stress.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:27.900
And two months later she died.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:32.832
And the worst part about it
is I wanted her gone so badly,

00:04:32.832 --> 00:04:35.000
and then when she was finally gone,

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.663
it wasn't what I wanted at all.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:40.810
- Wow.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:45.120
So my mom actually had
an alcohol problem too.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:46.160
Just initially hearing that,

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:47.570
I was immediately like triggered by it.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:50.570
I was like, "Oh," and then just
hearing what she had to say.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:52.880
I related to a lot of it,

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:54.750
not necessarily with the hopes

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:58.350
that my mom would go away more,
so I would say the opposite.

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.930
I lost my grandparents and I feel like

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:03.160
that kinda made her spiral a little bit,

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.610
so she was drinking a lot.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:07.390
That's what ultimately,
you know, killed her.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:09.570
Yeah, hearing that definitely.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:12.060
Yeah. Very similar stories I would say

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:14.210
- In 2020, my mother passed away

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:18.320
and ever since then it's only
really been my dad and I.

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:22.880
He has a lot of like anger
issues and he gets cranky a lot.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:27.360
He gets mad if you don't
do one thing for him.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.630
There are also other things he's done

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:30.760
before my mom passed away,

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:34.490
so there's just a lot of pent up anger

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:36.760
I also have towards him.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:40.130
Wishing death upon a
person is very strong,

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:43.280
but there have been times where I have

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.330
probably felt that way towards my father.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:49.610
- [Woman] My grandpa died two years ago

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:54.610
and I laughed because he
abused me when I was a child.

00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:57.733
- I've always wondered

00:05:57.733 --> 00:06:00.370
what it would be like when my dad passes.

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:03.560
I don't speak to him anymore
because he was very abusive.

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:06.080
Doesn't matter if they're
family, if they abuse you,

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:09.210
I mean, I don't know if I
would laugh when he passes.

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:10.710
It's sad when anyone dies,

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.480
but I don't even know if I'd be sad,

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:16.410
which is really sucks
because he is my dad.

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:19.200
I really miss the
relationship we used to have.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:20.900
- I don't really know what to say.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:28.020
I bet she just has this huge
weight lifted off her shoulders

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:31.210
that she doesn't have to
face this person anymore.

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:34.690
I'm guessing because that was
grandpa, she saw him a lot.

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:38.300
I'm angry that she was
abused and she was hurt.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:41.110
And not saying they
deserve to die in any way.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:43.320
I hope she can heal from that.

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:45.463
And if that brings her closure, then good.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:49.787
- [Woman] This November, I
found out I was pregnant.

00:06:49.787 --> 00:06:54.787
And at 12 weeks we found out
that we were having twins.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:07:00.900
And at that same appointment we found out

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:03.903
that our little girl was dead.

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:11.350
Our boy twin survived, but I just know

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:16.930
that everyone wanted a girl
and I couldn't keep her alive.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:24.320
I have been pregnant five
times with six children

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:29.610
and I have only brought
two into this world.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:33.593
I miss her every day.

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:36.433
I miss all my babies every day.

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:41.470
- I have been pregnant three times

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:45.150
and I have one son
that's alive here today.

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:49.510
I got pregnant at 19
and with my then husband

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:52.060
and I was eight months pregnant,

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:55.790
and I went to the
hospital and they told me

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:57.830
that they didn't hear a heartbeat.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.550
And so she was a stillborn,
so I still had to give birth

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:02.560
and go through the whole process.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.240
And I very much relate to that.

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:06.580
You know, still feeling that pain

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:10.023
that was in 2018, and when 2022 now.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:19.050
If there wasn't something wrong
with me that that happened,

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:23.890
that's my body that maybe
just the whole chain of events

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:25.580
wouldn't have happened.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:28.580
- Society has put on so
much pressure for women

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:33.500
to make sure that a
pregnancy all goes full term.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:36.110
I couldn't imagine all those losses

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:39.000
and all that guilt that weighs on her.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.090
And so I would tell that mom,
please don't punish yourself

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:44.260
for something that is out of your control

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:49.070
because I know you would
keep that child healthy

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:51.793
as long as possible and
forever, if you could.

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:57.799
- [Woman] When I was, I wanna say nine,

00:08:57.799 --> 00:09:00.780
my great uncle passed away.

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:02.700
Most people aren't super close

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.440
with their great uncles,
I guess, but I was.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:08.910
The last time I saw him,
we had got in an argument

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:11.230
'cause I was really young at the time

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:16.340
and I was throwing stuff
and he got really mad at me.

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:19.390
I just said, "I hate you."

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:23.130
And I've always regretted it.

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:26.310
I hate myself for saying that.

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:27.579
I miss him dearly.

00:09:27.579 --> 00:09:32.163
And yeah, I love you uncle Jack.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:34.957
- When you're little,

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:38.480
you don't realize the
weight that your words hold.

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:40.470
She was like eight, nine years old.

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:43.270
She didn't like expect that to happen

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:45.700
after she said that she hated him.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.760
I just really wish she didn't hate herself

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.650
'cause she didn't know.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:53.570
- When my sister passed,
it was so unexpected.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.120
She was perfectly healthy.

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:58.950
And I didn't think the day
that I last talked to her

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.630
would be the last day I talked to her.

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:02.540
Feeling like you didn't get closure

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:06.500
from the last interaction
you had with them.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:10.300
I mean, it's, it's really devastating.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:11.990
- My mom and I are more like best friends

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:15.200
than we are like mother and
daughter 'cause we're so close.

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:17.840
There have been times where
I'll like scream at her

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:18.990
and tell her I hate her,

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:20.760
and I don't want to talk to her anymore.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:25.760
And I've only seen my mom cry
like three times in my life

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:29.240
and I saw her cry after
an argument we had.

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:30.560
It was one of the three times,

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:33.600
and that's when I knew that
shouldn't have said that.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:35.530
Really hurt her feelings.

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:39.620
- [Woman] I am a very religious person

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:41.310
and I had a great grandfather

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:46.310
who I never truly knew if he
believed in the Lord or not.

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:50.010
And there was this one
time where I had a chance

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:52.110
to speak to him about it.

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:53.230
And I remember sitting there

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:56.200
and just having this pounding in my chest

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:58.453
saying, "Say something,
say something about it."

00:10:58.453 --> 00:10:59.960
And I never did.

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:02.340
And then a week later he passed away.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:05.200
And I fear that I could have been

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:08.930
his only door into salvation
if he hadn't found it already,

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:10.393
and I let it pass me up.

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:13.410
- I can relate to that.

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:15.730
I also grew up Christian.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:20.730
I know that feeling of
wanting and craving everyone

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.540
that's close to you to
have that connection

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:27.090
and that relationship
with God that you do.

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:28.710
I think in a way that there is

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:33.710
this sense of guilt within the church.

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:38.290
You're taught that if
you don't believe in it,

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:41.090
you're condemned to hell.

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:43.807
Kinda similar to what
she said of feeling like,

00:11:43.807 --> 00:11:47.180
"Oh I could have been
that salvation for him,"

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:49.810
but that's not up to us
at the end of the day.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:52.980
That's a choice that her grandfather made.

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:56.200
You know, that's something
that if he was at peace with,

00:11:56.200 --> 00:12:00.180
that's not something
she should have changed.

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:03.000
I think that she should
be at peace knowing that

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:06.783
wherever her grandfather did
go is where he intended to be.

00:12:07.839 --> 00:12:10.256
(calm music)

